filterFiles(filePaths: string[], options: FilterFilesOptions = {}): string[] {
  return filePaths.filter((filePath) => {
    const isDir = filePath.endsWith('/') || filePath.endsWith('\\');
    return !this._shouldIgnore(filePath, isDir, options);
  });
}
```

Note the source comment: directory paths must have a trailing slash to be matched against directory patterns `(e.g., 'dist/')`.

